  "title": "US and Iran Reopen Hormuz Strait Amid Global Security Tensions",
  "summary": "Iran and the U.S. have reopened the Strait of Hormuz, with Iran rejecting Trump's claim that the waterway will become U.S. territory, while the U.S. continues its blockade to weaken Iran's hold on the region. The conflict has stalled for over five months with both sides pushing for different approaches to resolve the crisis.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Iran's president denies threatening to resign during talks over the Strait of Hormuz, while the U.S. and Qatar report progress on a ceasefire and the reopening of the strait, though shipping remains blocked.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The conflict has stalled for over five months with both sides pushing for different approaches to resolve the crisis.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
